<!-- Monster Armor Page -->
<div data-role="page" class="jqm-demos jqm-home" id="monsterarmor">
  <%= erb :'sections/header' %>
  <%= erb :'sections/nav-panel' %>
  <%= erb :'sections/search-panel', locals: {loaded: @loaded} %>
  <% @loaded = 'true' %>
  
  <div role="main" class="ui-content">
    <div class="jqm-block-content">
      <h3>Monster Armor</h3>
      Some monsters have built-in Magic Armor, which is granted as a Trait. A monster that has four points of Monster armor will have <b>4pt (Magic)</b> written into their Armor line.<br><br>
      Monster Armor:
      <ol>
        <li>Behaves identically to magic armor.</li>
        <li>Cannot be combined with other types of armor.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><i><a href="#monster-abilities">All Monster Abilities & Mechanics</a></i></p>
    </div>
  </div><!-- /content -->
</div><!-- Monster Armor /page -->

<!-- Inherent Enchantments Page -->
<div data-role="page" class="jqm-demos jqm-home" id="inherentenchantments">
  <%= erb :'sections/header' %>
  <%= erb :'sections/nav-panel' %>
  <%= erb :'sections/search-panel', locals: {loaded: @loaded} %>
  <% @loaded = 'true' %>
  
  <div role="main" class="ui-content">
    <div class="jqm-block-content">
      <h3>Inherent Enchantments</h3>
      These Enchantments are automatically cast upon a monster when they start a scenario, respawn, or cast Sheer Numbers. For example, a monster may be written as having <b>Gift of Air (i)</b>. Inherent enchantments differ from Traits in that they can be Dispelled or removed and should be announced upon engagement with other players. If a player is already at their Enchantment limit when an Inherent enchantment would be applied, they may choose which Enchantment(s) to lose to meet their Enchantment limit.
      <p><i><a href="#monster-abilities">All Monster Abilities & Mechanics</a></i></p>
    </div>
  </div><!-- /content -->
</div><!-- Inherent Enchantments /page -->

